{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/672019-tv-set-troubles","id":672019,"title":"TV Set Troubles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-20T08:39:16-07:00","id":672019,"title":"TV Set Troubles","content":"So, for years now, I've had a 40&quot; Philips LCD that I got a great deal for, as it was a floor model, and it's worked fine for all that time. Just a few days ago, the picture started breaking up, freezing and fading out, until whenever I turned on the TV, it would soon fade into a grayish-white screen (sound still worked fine). <br /> <br /> I had a repair guy out to look at it, he identified the problem being a certain circuit board or something, that would cost $180-200 to fix. At that point, I figure I may as well get a new TV, as this one would probably blow something else soon anyway. <br /> <br /> The next day, I spend all day driving around to various places, looking for a cheap 40&quot; LED with 1080 resolution and 120 refresh rate, which my Philips has. Turns out the closest I come is a store right down the block from me, which I should've checked first anyway!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, I bite the bullet and buy a new TV (Doctor Who was premiering!); the only thing it's missing is the 120 rr, which the salesman says is almost impossible to find on a non-smart TV these days, and I like my TVs good and dumb, thank you very much. Anyway, I get it home and set it up, and it looks great (minus the 120 Smooth Motion). I want to compare it to my old one, so I plug that back in, to get one last look at the picture before it fades to gray again...<br /> <br /> ...only it never did. I kept it on for hours, all-day, waiting for the screen to fade away, but, it played great. Watched DW and a few more things before going to bed, and it worked as well as it ever has.<br /> <br /> So, now I have two TVs, which is one too many. Do I take back the new one, and stick with the old? Or toss the old one anyway, and commit fully to the new?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:10:11-07:00","id":672267,"title":"","content":"Fully commit to the new one. ....when the old one dies again. Until then, stick with the classic dumb tv.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T17:02:10-07:00","id":672502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/672019-tv-set-troubles?p=672267#post672267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fully commit to the new one. ....when the old one dies again. Until then, stick with the classic dumb tv.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I keep buying a new tv once a year or so, start missing my grandma's RCA analog 22&quot; from the late 70s with the wooden frame, and then just giving the new one to whatever relative needs a tv so I can go back to it.<br /> <br /> I'm watching that RCA right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T21:27:10-07:00","id":676002,"title":"","content":"Ok, well, the old actually crapped out again shortly after making my last post, so I've just went ahead and hooked up the new one full-on. <br /> <br /> NOW, my issue is: My job is offering special employee discounts for TVs, one of which matches all my wants/needs! It's all this new one is, plus 120 hertz, PLUS a smart TV! And it's only about 20 bucks more. That's only for 2 days, sooo...if it's still there, I think I'm gonna get it and take this new one back.<br /> [crosses tentacles]<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T08:46:19-07:00","id":689763,"title":"","content":"...Aaand that's exactly what I did, with no problems (just needed a spot of financial assistance)! New set works great, sounds great, works with the soundbar, and lets me get to Netflix with the touch of a button. The *only* thing it doesn't do, despite being 120 hrtz, is that &quot;smooth motion&quot; visual effect that I really liked from the old one, which is weird. Anywho, that's one less of my 99 problems to deal with...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}